    "blurb": "The show bursts with a sparkling Keith mix and Jerry on fire throughout. Highlights include a transcendent Bird Song, a monster The Other One, and tight jams on Playing In The Band > Truckin'. Overall performance is high‑energy and the soundboard capture is clear and complete.",
    "review": "December 12, 1972 at Winterland finds the Dead in peak form, delivering a setlist that swings from tight early‑rockers to expansive second‑set improvisations. Jerry’s guitar soars on Bird Song and The Other One, while Phil lays down a solid bass foundation that could use a touch more presence in the mix. Keith’s piano is unusually forward, adding sparkle to every jam, and Bob’s weathered vocals lend character—even when his voice sounds a little hoarse. The second set builds momentum with a powerful Playing In The Band > Truckin' transition into a marathon The Other One that showcases the band’s collective chemistry. A crisp soundboard recording captures all of this with minimal splices, making it one of the more accessible Winterland documents from the early‑’70s.",
